      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STERN DISPUTE (4) brings the clearest winning profile after a well-supported second at Casino, where he was beaten just over a length by Airhawk, and that followed a BM58 win at Grafton over SUNSET TRAIL. The slight rise in trip is no issue and he rates highly on the back of his latest performance. DOINGITEASY (5) is the main danger on consistency, coming off a CL1 third at Ipswich after another placing behind Airhawk at Grafton, and his record at around 1595m reads well. CAISHEN (3) has been around the mark in stronger recent company, finishing fourth in a BM62 at Sunshine Coast after a narrow CL1 second to King Emperor, so he appeals as a solid placing and winning hope if the quick back-up is no issue. MAURRAQA (6) has to stretch to around 1595m for the first time, but he gets weight relief, has won at this track and is third-up with a more suitable profile than his past two results suggest. SUNSET TRAIL (2) won't be far away.",
